      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "It's mostly at night. I wake up with the pins and needles in my fingers, and I have to shake them out over the side of the bed.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:23",
      "end_timestamp": "00:37",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Ah, let me think. Since after Christmas. About eight weeks. Or maybe nine, I lose track of the weeks since I retired.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:53",
      "end_timestamp": "01:06",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "In the morning my fingers are numb, like they're not mine. It wears off once I've had my tea. And I'm after dropping a cup twice this week, which is not like me.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:19",
      "end_timestamp": "01:37",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "The tablets help at night, I'd say. Better than before. The pregabalin, 75 mg, one at night. That's what I take.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:10",
      "end_timestamp": "02:20",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "The vitamin B12, the tablets, 1000 micrograms. Once a day, with breakfast. Or is it with dinner? I take it with breakfast.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:30",
      "end_timestamp": "02:43",
      "supports": [
        "medications[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
